tains live cultures and organic acids; naturally low sugar (<2g/12 oz) Variability in sugar content\u2014always check label; higher price point $3.49\u2013$4.99/bottle Herbal Iced Tea (brewed, no sweetener) Caffeine sensitivity, hydration qualityNo phosphoric acid; rich in polyphenols; customizable Requires preparation time; tannins may inhibit non-heme iron absorption if consumed with meals $0.15\u2013$0.30/serving (home-brewed) Diet Pepsi Immediate sugar reduction, taste familiarityZero sugar, consistent formulation, broad distribution Artificial sweeteners, low pH, no nutritional value $1.29\u2013$1.89/can Regular Pepsi Acute energy need (e.g., hypoglycemia)Rapid glucose delivery, predictable dosing High added sugar, enamel demineralization, displaces nutrient-dense fluids $1.29\u2013$1.89/can Visual comparison of beverage options\u2014from most supportive (left) to least supportive (right)\u2014based on sugar, acid, sweetener type, and nutrient density. \ud83d\udce3 Customer Feedback Synthesis Analysis of verified consumer reviews (across major retailers and health forums, Jan\u2013Jun 2024) reveals consistent themes: \u2b50 Frequent positive feedback : \u201cHelped me cut 100+ sugar calories daily\u201d; \u201cTastes nearly identical to regular Pepsi\u201d; \u201cNo energy crash like with sugary drinks.\u201d \u2757 Recurring concerns : \u201cGave me headaches after 3 days\u201d; \u201cMade me crave sweets more intensely\u201d; \u201cCaused bloating and indigestion\u201d; \u201cTaste became metallic over time.\u201d \ud83d\udcdd Notable nuance : Users reporting neutral or positive outcomes overwhelmingly described concurrent behavior changes\u2014e.g., pairing Diet Pepsi with protein-rich snacks, drinking it only before noon, or using it strictly as a transitional tool (\u22646 weeks). \u26a0\ufe0f Maintenance, Safety & Legal Considerations Neither Diet Pepsi nor Pepsi requires special maintenance\u2014both are shelf-stable until opened. Post-opening, refrigera